much as it challenges them

00:10:50.117 --> 00:10:51.367
to get started.

00:10:53.328 --> 00:10:57.161
Getting started is
absolutely the key to life.

00:10:58.968 --> 00:11:01.352
And, by the time I finished
going through this personal

00:11:01.352 --> 00:11:03.513
growth kit, by the time
that was all finished,

00:11:03.513 --> 00:11:06.919
I had six months of day in,
day out personal growth.

00:11:06.919 --> 00:11:10.193
And what it did is it
developed a habit in my life

00:11:10.193 --> 00:11:12.273
and by the time I finished with that kit,

00:11:12.273 --> 00:11:16.135
now I'm used to spending time
every day in personal growth.

00:11:16.135 --> 00:11:17.635
It got me started.

00:11:20.179 --> 00:11:23.283
I mean, this is worth this
whole lesson if you could

00:11:23.283 --> 00:11:24.450
just get this.

00:11:26.162 --> 00:11:28.890
The reason why I'm so
passionate about personal growth

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:31.973
is personal growth keeps me prepared.

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.900
In other words, if I'm continuing growing

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:38.317
and I'm continually developing myself

00:11:38.317 --> 00:11:40.817
and I'm continually
learning, and I'm continually

00:11:40.817 --> 00:11:43.438
doing new things and going
to another step higher,

00:11:43.438 --> 00:11:44.907
can I tell you what that is?

00:11:44.907 --> 00:11:48.000
That constant growth is the
preparation for the opportunity

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:52.568
so when the opportunity
comes, here's the way,

00:11:52.568 --> 00:11:55.598
you don't go into an opportunity,

00:11:55.598 --> 00:11:58.015
you grow into an opportunity.

00:12:00.553 --> 00:12:01.924
And so, I'm passionate
about personal growth

00:12:01.924 --> 00:12:04.242
because for that person who
says, wow, I had an opportunity.

00:12:04.242 --> 00:12:06.136
I wasn't ready.

00:12:06.136 --> 00:12:09.118
If you're growing you're
always ready because after I

00:12:09.118 --> 00:12:13.375
intentionally started
growing, I made a commitment

00:12:13.375 --> 00:12:14.944
to grow as a leader.

00:12:14.944 --> 00:12:17.240
I started writing, I became and author.

00:12:17.240 --> 00:12:19.582
I developed growth
resources for other people.

00:12:19.582 --> 00:12:21.114
I founded my first company.

00:12:21.114 --> 00:12:22.633
I began training conferences.

00:12:22.633 --> 00:12:24.341
Everything I could think
of that has ever been good

00:12:24.341 --> 00:12:26.719
in my life was a result
of the fact that I started

00:12:26.719 --> 00:12:29.702
personal growth in my life.

00:12:29.702 --> 00:12:31.035
I got started and guess what?

00:12:31.035 --> 00:12:32.625
When I got started, let me
tell you what I didn't have.

00:12:32.625 --> 00:12:34.009
I didn't have experience.

00:12:34.009 --> 00:12:35.114
I didn't have knowledge.

00:12:35.114 --> 00:12:36.287
I did not have a motto.

00:12:36.287 --> 00:12:37.408
I did not have a mentor.

00:12:37.408 --> 00:12:38.410
I did not have a plan.

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:39.944
I did not have a fellow traveler.

00:12:39.944 --> 00:12:41.213
I did not have resources.

00:12:41.213 --> 00:12:42.190
I did not have money.

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:45.190
I did not have a growth environment.

00:12:48.269 --> 00:12:49.852
But, I got started.

00:12:53.321 --> 00:12:57.488
You don't stop or not start
because of what you don't have.

00:13:01.757 --> 00:13:06.058
You don't start because
you don't realize yet

00:13:06.058 --> 00:13:09.475
that the fruit of everything good in life

00:13:13.109 --> 00:13:15.109
begins with a challenge.

00:13:16.202 --> 00:13:19.889
There's nothing easy in
life worthwhile in life.

00:13:19.889 --> 00:13:23.139
Everything is a pill that's worthwhile.

00:13:24.067 --> 00:13:27.150
And it's not going to come to
you and it's not going to fall

00:13:27.150 --> 00:13:29.414
in your lap and it's not
going to be something that,

00:13:29.414 --> 00:13:32.093
oh my God, it just was so simple.

00:13:32.093 --> 00:13:35.414
It's always going to be difficult.

00:13:35.414 --> 00:13:38.980
The rule of five is the
most life changing concept

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:43.205
for focusing on success
that I have ever taught,

00:13:43.205 --> 00:13:46.523
that I have ever lived so I'm
just going to drop it on you

00:13:46.523 --> 00:13:49.079
just enough to help you
understand the five concept,

00:13:49.079 --> 00:13:51.299
to help you understand the
five things you need to do

00:13:51.299 --> 00:13:53.286
to lift your leadership lid.

00:13:53.286 --> 00:13:55.541
The rule of five just simply
says, if you have a tree

00:13:55.541 --> 00:13:59.120
in your background that
you want to cut down

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:03.080
and you have an ax, if
everyday you pick up that ax

00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:06.137
and you go to that tree
and you swing five times

00:14:06.137 --> 00:14:10.054
with that ax to hit that
tree, put the ax down.

00:14:11.921 --> 00:14:13.825
The next day you go out, pick up the ax,

00:14:13.825 --> 00:14:17.658
swing five times at the
tree, put the ax down.

00:14:21.413 --> 00:14:23.028
The next day you go out, pick up the ax

00:14:23.028 --> 00:14:25.488
and five more times
you swing at that tree,

00:14:25.488 --> 00:14:27.799
five times, everyday, you pick up the ax

00:14:27.799 --> 00:14:28.817
and only five.

00:14:28.817 --> 00:14:31.082
Not 50, not 15, not 500.

00:14:31.082 --> 00:14:34.624
If you swing five times a day at that tree

00:14:34.624 --> 00:14:36.971
with that ax everyday,
let me ask you a question,

00:14:36.971 --> 00:14:39.442
what eventually is going
to happen to that tree?

00:14:39.442 --> 00:14:40.788
That tree is going to?

00:14:40.788 --> 00:14:42.708
- [Audience] Fall.

00:14:42.708 --> 00:14:43.975
- Now, there's no question about that.

00:14:43.975 --> 00:14:45.212
Is there?

00:14:45.212 --> 00:14:46.315
There isn't any doubt.

00:14:46.315 --> 00:14:47.425
You don't have to sit around the table

00:14:47.425 --> 00:14:48.908
and kind of say, do you think it will?

00:14:48.908 --> 00:14:50.569
(audience laughing)

00:14:50.569 --> 00:14:52.676
Hmm, let's hold hands and
sing kumbaya and hope.

00:14:52.676 --> 00:14:55.676
(audience laughing)

00:15:03.404 --> 00:15:07.226
If you swing five times a
day at that tree everyday,

00:15:07.226 --> 00:15:09.976
that tree will fall in the story.

00:15:11.991 --> 00:15:16.158
Now, if it's a big tree,
it may take a couple years.

00:15:17.827 --> 00:15:19.520
If it's a little tree in
your backyard, I don't know,

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:21.614
maybe in a month you could
knock that baby down.

00:15:21.614 --> 00:15:24.808
See, now the size of
the tree will determine

00:15:24.808 --> 00:15:27.581
how long it takes for it to fall.

00:15:27.581 --> 00:15:29.525
But that's not what we're debating here.

00:15:29.525 --> 00:15:31.757
What we're teaching here
is if you swing five times

00:15:31.757 --> 00:15:35.924
a day at that tree, every
day, the tree will fall.

00:15:40.041 --> 00:15:42.462
Now, that's the rule of five.

00:15:42.462 --> 00:15:45.545
The rule of five says find your tree.

00:15:47.087 --> 00:15:49.074
What's your goal in life?

00:15:49.074 --> 00:15:50.802
What's your purpose?

00:15:50.802 --> 00:15:52.758
What do you want to accomplish?

00:15:52.758 --> 00:15:55.473
What do you want to knock down?

00:15:55.473 --> 00:15:57.456
Where's your ax?

00:15:57.456 --> 00:15:59.586
What are your tools?

00:15:59.586 --> 00:16:02.084
What is it that you're
going to use to effectively

00:16:02.084 --> 00:16:05.535
go after that goal five times a day?

00:16:05.535 --> 00:16:06.513
What are you?

00:16:06.513 --> 00:16:07.754
What is it because whatever that is,

00:16:07.754 --> 00:16:11.754
whatever that is, if you
use it five times a day

00:16:13.464 --> 00:16:16.714
every day, you'll be highly successful.

00:16:17.841 --> 00:16:20.612
For example, I write books.

00:16:20.612 --> 00:16:22.790
So let me just put that
in writing for a moment.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.623
I've written 73 books.

00:16:25.787 --> 00:16:28.476
Jason, that was a nice
introduction it's 22 million,

00:16:28.476 --> 00:16:29.496
not 19.

00:16:29.496 --> 00:16:31.933
(audience laughing)

00:16:31.933 --> 00:16:33.834
But, what's two or three million?

00:16:33.834 --> 00:16:36.143
(audience laughing)

00:16:36.143 --> 00:16:40.310
Give a little, take a little,
little here, little there.

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:46.604
People say, John, how
have you written 73 books?

00:16:46.604 --> 00:16:48.360
Oh, thank you for asking.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:51.420
(audience laughing)

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:52.837
The rule of five.

00:16:54.181 --> 00:16:57.848
You see, there are five
things I do everyday

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:01.622
that allows me to write that many books.

00:17:01.622 --> 00:17:02.872
It's not magic.

00:17:03.718 --> 00:17:06.051
It's not that I'm brilliant.

00:17:07.118 --> 00:17:10.276
It's just that I know the rule of five.

00:17:10.276 --> 00:17:12.047
The rule of five.

00:17:12.047 --> 00:17:14.787
You see, everyday I read.

00:17:14.787 --> 00:17:16.105
Every day I file.

00:17:16.105 --> 00:17:17.612
Every day I think.

00:17:17.612 --> 00:17:19.840
Every day I ask questions
and every day I write.

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:20.816
Every day.

00:17:20.816 --> 00:17:21.793
I do those five things every day.

00:17:21.793 --> 00:17:24.071
Every day I read, every day
I file, every day I think,

00:17:24.071 --> 00:17:25.773
every day I ask questions,
every day I write,

00:17:25.773 --> 00:17:27.832
every day I read, every day
I think, every day I file,

00:17:27.832 --> 00:17:29.227
every day I ask questions,
every day I write,

00:17:29.227 --> 00:17:30.855
every day I think, every day I read,

00:17:30.855 --> 00:17:32.380
every day I ask questions,
every day I file,

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:34.277
every day I write, every day I write,

00:17:34.277 --> 00:17:36.016
every day I read, every day
I think, every day I file,

00:17:36.016 --> 00:17:37.267
every day I ask questions.

00:17:37.267 --> 00:17:40.143
Yes, I can do it in different
orders but every day.

00:17:40.143 --> 00:17:41.901
Doesn't matter whether you
swing the ax left handed

00:17:41.901 --> 00:17:45.507
or right handed, you
just got to hit the tree.

00:17:45.507 --> 00:17:49.674
Every day I read, file,
think, ask questions, write,

00:17:50.584 --> 00:17:52.965
read, think, file, ask
questions, write, read, think,

00:17:52.965 --> 00:17:55.357
file, ask questions, write.

00:17:55.357 --> 00:17:57.526
You say now John, what
do you mean by every day?

00:17:57.526 --> 00:18:00.526
(audience laughing)

00:18:01.631 --> 00:18:03.915
This is where it gets a
little long sometimes.

00:18:03.915 --> 00:18:05.433
(audience laughing)

00:18:05.433 --> 00:18:08.600
What I mean by every day is every day.

00:18:10.329 --> 00:18:12.502
Now you say, now when you say every day

00:18:12.502 --> 00:18:15.378
do you mean that you do that on Sunday?

00:18:15.378 --> 00:18:17.745
Every Sunday I read, think,
file, ask questions, write.

00:18:17.745 --> 00:18:20.914
Do you do that on your
birthday every birthday?

00:18:20.914 --> 00:18:22.739
Guess what, every birthday
I read, think, file,

00:18:22.739 --> 00:18:23.831
ask questions, write.

00:18:23.831 --> 00:18:25.151
Do you do that on Christmas?

00:18:25.151 --> 00:18:26.555
Guess what I do every Christmas?

00:18:26.555 --> 00:18:29.125
Every Christmas I read, think,
file, ask questions, write.

00:18:29.125 --> 00:18:30.923
Do you do this when you're feeling well?

00:18:30.923 --> 00:18:32.377
Can I tell you when I'm not feeling well,

00:18:32.377 --> 00:18:34.165
even if I'm not feeling well
guess what I do every day?

00:18:34.165 --> 00:18:37.385
When I'm not feeling well I
think, write, ask questions,

00:18:37.385 --> 00:18:39.968
do all those things, every day.

00:18:42.159 --> 00:18:43.742
You say, every day?

00:18:48.422 --> 00:18:52.046
At the age of 17, I started filing.

00:18:52.046 --> 00:18:54.668
I've never missed a day.

00:18:54.668 --> 00:18:56.237
I don't have 100 quotes.

00:18:56.237 --> 00:18:58.191
I don't have 1,000 quotes.

00:18:58.191 --> 00:19:00.747
I have tens of thousands of quotes.

00:19:00.747 --> 00:19:01.822
I don't have 100 stories.

00:19:01.822 --> 00:19:02.972
I don't have a 1,000 stories.

00:19:02.972 --> 00:19:04.386
I have 10,000 stories.

00:19:04.386 --> 00:19:05.404
Where did you get all those stories?

00:19:05.404 --> 00:19:06.381
Where'd you get all those quotes?

00:19:06.381 --> 00:19:07.357
Well, let me tell you something.

00:19:07.357 --> 00:19:09.136
Guess what I do every day?

00:19:09.136 --> 00:19:11.442
(audience laughing)

00:19:11.442 --> 00:19:15.109
See, we overestimate
what we can do in a day

00:19:16.413 --> 00:19:20.580
and we underestimate what
we can do in several days.

00:19:22.198 --> 00:19:23.669
And you got to understand,
you got to understand,

00:19:23.669 --> 00:19:26.251
the secret of success is
not the fact that hey,

00:19:26.251 --> 00:19:29.620
I didn't say, hey, some
days I get up and I write

00:19:29.620 --> 00:19:31.106
for 12 hours.

00:19:31.106 --> 00:19:33.338
No, no, no, no, no.

00:19:33.338 --> 00:19:35.183
I didn't say I write all day.

00:19:35.183 --> 00:19:36.381
I didn't say I read all day.

00:19:36.381 --> 00:19:37.424
I didn't say I think all day.

00:19:37.424 --> 00:19:38.518
I didn't say I ask questions all day.

00:19:38.518 --> 00:19:40.335
I just said every day, every day.

00:19:40.335 --> 00:19:43.023
You see, doing a little
bit every day is a lot

00:19:43.023 --> 00:19:46.440
more important than doing a lot some day.

00:19:47.461 --> 00:19:50.720
And most people live in some day.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:52.242
Well I tell ya what, I
think I'll get to that.

00:19:52.242 --> 00:19:53.375
You know what, I think I'll try that.

00:19:53.375 --> 00:19:54.627
You know what, I believe I (mumbles).

00:19:54.627 --> 00:19:55.649
Now, now here's the key.

00:19:55.649 --> 00:19:59.134
You got to figure out what the five are.

00:19:59.134 --> 00:20:03.210
It took me seven years to
find my five for writing.

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.710
John, you're slow.

00:20:05.888 --> 00:20:07.535
(audience laughing)

00:20:07.535 --> 00:20:08.717
I am.

00:20:08.717 --> 00:20:11.134
It won't take you seven years

00:20:12.498 --> 00:20:14.651
but it'll take you a long period of time.

00:20:14.651 --> 00:20:16.140
I can get the first two
quickly but the third,

00:20:16.140 --> 00:20:18.137
the fourth, the fifth,
it took me four years

00:20:18.137 --> 00:20:19.841
to get the last one.

00:20:19.841 --> 00:20:22.495
I can remember as a
parent as my children got

00:20:22.495 --> 00:20:27.276
to a certain age and where they
looked to me for influence.

00:20:27.276 --> 00:20:29.354
I can remember very well
when I saw them beginning

00:20:29.354 --> 00:20:31.872
to go to their friends.

00:20:31.872 --> 00:20:34.209
And that's where the influence
began and that's where

00:20:34.209 --> 00:20:35.549
their influence began to increase.

00:20:35.549 --> 00:20:37.347
As a parent that got a little scary for me

00:20:37.347 --> 00:20:40.109
because I could see I was
having a little less influence

00:20:40.109 --> 00:20:43.417
and the friends were
having a little bit more.

00:20:43.417 --> 00:20:46.207
But my parents were very wise.

00:20:46.207 --> 00:20:49.375
My parents understood
that who my friends were

00:20:49.375 --> 00:20:51.276
would determine who I was going to become.

00:20:51.276 --> 00:20:53.665
Birds of a feather flock together.

00:20:53.665 --> 00:20:56.207
And in their wisdom they
decided that they wanted to know

00:20:56.207 --> 00:20:59.501
my friends and they
wanted to see my friends.

00:20:59.501 --> 00:21:01.637
So therefore, they provided
a lot of wonderful things

00:21:01.637 --> 00:21:04.547
at our home so we would have
our friends at our house

00:21:04.547 --> 00:21:07.261
so that my parents could
observe and watch the kind

00:21:07.261 --> 00:21:10.652
of kids I ran around with
and what I learned as a kid

00:21:10.652 --> 00:21:12.819
growing up is very simple.

00:21:13.921 --> 00:21:16.398
There are some friends
that were positive for me.

00:21:16.398 --> 00:21:19.271
There were some friends
that were negative for me

00:21:19.271 --> 00:21:21.817
and my determination of which
friends I was going to let

00:21:21.817 --> 00:21:24.912
influence me basically
determined whether I was

00:21:24.912 --> 00:21:28.242
going to have a positive
or a negative life.

00:21:28.242 --> 00:21:31.711
Fortunately, because of good
parental advice and guidance,

00:21:31.711 --> 00:21:35.584
I chose good friends which
really did make a difference

00:21:35.584 --> 00:21:38.868
because, you see, friends are wonderful.

00:21:38.868 --> 00:21:41.421
They give us support,
they give us strength.

00:21:41.421 --> 00:21:46.184
They're either though a
real asset or real liability

00:21:46.184 --> 00:21:49.019
so I would just want to encourage you,

00:21:49.019 --> 00:21:51.710
choose your friends wisely.

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:55.431
You don't need a lot but
you need some good ones.

00:21:55.431 --> 00:21:57.922
Every leader I have
ever known had a dream,

00:21:57.922 --> 00:21:59.640
had a vision.

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:02.903
In fact, I would say to
you if you're not seeing

00:22:02.903 --> 00:22:05.566
what could be and what
you would like to have,

00:22:05.566 --> 00:22:09.080
I would say you probably are not a leader.

00:22:09.080 --> 00:22:11.979
But what I've discovered
about dreams is this,

00:22:11.979 --> 00:22:15.146
dreams are free but the journey isn't.

00:22:17.178 --> 00:22:20.641
And so, leaders go beyond
just having a dream.

00:22:20.641 --> 00:22:23.483
They go beyond having a
wish list, sitting around

00:22:23.483 --> 00:22:27.379
a table and kind of hoping
something might come to pass.

00:22:27.379 --> 00:22:29.691
They understand that if they have a dream,

00:22:29.691 --> 00:22:33.522
if they're a dreamer,
they have to pursue that.

00:22:33.522 --> 00:22:35.907
They have to take the journey.

00:22:35.907 --> 00:22:38.857
The dream's free, the journey isn't.

00:22:38.857 --> 00:22:41.755
And what leaders find is
that when they go forth

00:22:41.755 --> 00:22:44.846
toward that dream, they
continually have to pay

00:22:44.846 --> 00:22:46.476
that price.

00:22:46.476 --> 00:22:49.159
They continually have to
realize that they make

00:22:49.159 --> 00:22:52.844
down payments on the dream they have.

00:22:52.844 --> 00:22:55.688
But there's one thing
else I would like to say,

00:22:55.688 --> 00:22:58.718
all leaders realize that
whatever they pay, it's worth

00:22:58.718 --> 00:23:03.600
the price because dreams,
for them, do come true.

00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:06.385
I was sitting at a round
table with executives one day

00:23:06.385 --> 00:23:10.069
and a person that is highly
successful I could tell

00:23:10.069 --> 00:23:11.526
was a little discouraged.

00:23:11.526 --> 00:23:13.749
He said, John, I've hit
every goal in my life

00:23:13.749 --> 00:23:18.720
and now I basically have lost
my motivation and my passion.

00:23:18.720 --> 00:23:20.338
And I looked at him, I called him by name.

00:23:20.338 --> 00:23:21.315
I'll say Don.

00:23:21.315 --> 00:23:23.022
That wasn't his name.

00:23:23.022 --> 00:23:27.344
I said, Don, the problem is
you've been goal oriented

00:23:27.344 --> 00:23:29.305
instead of growth oriented.

00:23:29.305 --> 00:23:31.116
You see, if you and
are just goal oriented,

00:23:31.116 --> 00:23:33.227
when we hit our goals
it's kind of like, eureka,

00:23:33.227 --> 00:23:34.203
we've arrived.

00:23:34.203 --> 00:23:35.826
We celebrate, have a party
but then all of a sudden

00:23:35.826 --> 00:23:37.667
there's an emptiness
like okay, I've hit it.

00:23:37.667 --> 00:23:42.490
But if you're growth
oriented and establish goals

00:23:42.490 --> 00:23:46.371
within your growth oriented
journey, you'll hit those goals

00:23:46.371 --> 00:23:48.678
but you'll at it and say hey,
this is just another step

00:23:48.678 --> 00:23:51.707
towards my total growth and
I've never known a person

00:23:51.707 --> 00:23:55.262
who said, John, I've grown
as big as I could ever grow

00:23:55.262 --> 00:23:57.879
and I know as much as I could
ever know and so therefore

00:23:57.879 --> 00:23:59.526
I have nothing to accomplish.

00:23:59.526 --> 00:24:02.155
You see, if you're goal
oriented, you'll hit your goal

00:24:02.155 --> 00:24:04.675
and then be a little empty
but if you're growth oriented,

00:24:04.675 --> 00:24:07.750
you'll never hit that goal.

00:24:07.750 --> 00:24:09.250
Just keep growing.

00:24:10.204 --> 00:24:14.313
You and I both know that God's
gift to us if our potential

00:24:14.313 --> 00:24:19.141
and our gift back to him is
what we do with our potential.

00:24:19.141 --> 00:24:22.502
Perhaps the greatest insult
that we could ever give

00:24:22.502 --> 00:24:25.335
to our creator is to be a slacker.

00:24:26.500 --> 00:24:29.890
To somehow have these gifts
and have these opportunities

00:24:29.890 --> 00:24:33.920
and have this potential
and do nothing with it.

00:24:33.920 --> 00:24:36.956
I would suggest today that
you believe in yourself

00:24:36.956 --> 00:24:39.420
as much as God believes in you.

00:24:39.420 --> 00:24:41.638
He created you for greatness.

00:24:41.638 --> 00:24:44.221
Now, that's how he created you.

00:24:45.213 --> 00:24:47.806
You determine how great you become.

00:24:47.806 --> 00:24:50.097
He has already given you the
potential and he's already

00:24:50.097 --> 00:24:52.291
given you the opportunity.

00:24:52.291 --> 00:24:55.865
Your response, either
seize the moment in the day

00:24:55.865 --> 00:24:58.223
and become all that you possibly can be

00:24:58.223 --> 00:25:01.280
or slack in the moment and
basically rest and just let

00:25:01.280 --> 00:25:03.688
things come to you.

00:25:03.688 --> 00:25:06.520
I encourage you on Minute with Maxwell,

00:25:06.520 --> 00:25:09.250
take the potential that you
have been given as a gift

00:25:09.250 --> 00:25:12.479
and the way to say thanks to that gift

00:25:12.479 --> 00:25:15.646
is by giving your life your very best.

00:25:16.644 --> 00:25:18.898
And the word that came
to my heart this year

00:25:18.898 --> 00:25:21.430
that I think God wants
me to focus on in 2015

00:25:21.430 --> 00:25:23.430
is the word intentional.

00:25:25.366 --> 00:25:28.313
He wants me to be intentional.

00:25:28.313 --> 00:25:31.073
He wants me to, maybe more
than ever before in my life

00:25:31.073 --> 00:25:34.270
really focus on some
things that are important

00:25:34.270 --> 00:25:38.982
and live a life everyday
not a day that kind of where

00:25:38.982 --> 00:25:42.110
I try to accept my day but
a day where I lead my day.

00:25:42.110 --> 00:25:46.277
A day where I focus on
making sure I really, really

00:25:47.515 --> 00:25:50.210
put my intentionality
where it needs to be.

00:25:50.210 --> 00:25:52.487
We all heard the expression,
all is well that ends well.

00:25:52.487 --> 00:25:57.053
I'm hear to tell you all
is well that begins well.

00:25:57.053 --> 00:25:58.841
And this is the first of
the year and for many of you

00:25:58.841 --> 00:26:00.434
this is your chance.

00:26:00.434 --> 00:26:01.870
This is your shot.

00:26:01.870 --> 00:26:02.911
This is your moment.

00:26:02.911 --> 00:26:04.356
This is your time.

00:26:04.356 --> 00:26:06.439
This is your opportunity.

00:26:07.975 --> 00:26:10.736
All of you that are watching
online, the different campuses,

00:26:10.736 --> 00:26:13.047
Day Star, this is your opportunity.

00:26:13.047 --> 00:26:14.024
This is your time.

00:26:14.024 --> 00:26:14.999
This is your moment.

00:26:14.999 --> 00:26:16.499
This is your place

00:26:17.734 --> 00:26:21.901
for you to really begin to
live an intentional life.

