00:27:13.399 --> 00:27:16.183
- People that are
knowledgeable about habits

00:27:16.183 --> 00:27:20.350
say that it takes 30 days for
a habit to become a habit.

00:27:21.275 --> 00:27:23.950
In other words, you and I
can't, in one or two days,

00:27:23.950 --> 00:27:25.601
develop a habit.

00:27:25.601 --> 00:27:26.956
It takes a long time.

00:27:26.956 --> 00:27:29.712
In fact, I am prone to think
it takes a little longer

00:27:29.712 --> 00:27:31.147
than 30 days.

00:27:31.147 --> 00:27:33.878
Now, habits can be good
and habits can be bad

00:27:33.878 --> 00:27:35.795
and so over a period of time

00:27:35.795 --> 00:27:38.087
you can either be developing
habits that are going to help you

00:27:38.087 --> 00:27:39.974
or you're going to be
developing habits that are going

00:27:39.974 --> 00:27:40.951
to hurt you.

00:27:40.951 --> 00:27:45.609
People that grow develop
habits that help them.

00:27:45.609 --> 00:27:48.516
The great value of a good
habit is you don't have

00:27:48.516 --> 00:27:50.394
to think about it,
that's why it's a habit.

00:27:50.394 --> 00:27:53.565
In other words, once you
begin to over days and times

00:27:53.565 --> 00:27:56.496
and periods, begin to practice
something that's good,

00:27:56.496 --> 00:27:59.626
after a while it becomes automatic to you.

00:27:59.626 --> 00:28:01.000
It becomes who you are.

00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:04.677
In fact, I always tell
people, practice a good habit

00:28:04.677 --> 00:28:08.343
long enough to make it
yours and once it's yours

00:28:08.343 --> 00:28:12.510
now it's automatic, everyday,
you'll do what you should do.

00:28:14.147 --> 00:28:16.232
I heard a story this week
about a lady who bought

00:28:16.232 --> 00:28:19.556
a parrot at the store and
she was kind of lonely

00:28:19.556 --> 00:28:21.794
so she wanted the parrot to
kind of take home to talk

00:28:21.794 --> 00:28:22.769
to her.

00:28:22.769 --> 00:28:25.009
So she took the parrot home
and sat there and you know,

00:28:25.009 --> 00:28:29.088
the parrot in the cage, the
parrot didn't say a word.

00:28:29.088 --> 00:28:30.391
The next day she went to
the store and she said,

00:28:30.391 --> 00:28:32.041
the parrot doesn't talk.

00:28:32.041 --> 00:28:33.823
Well, the manager at the
store said, well, you know,

00:28:33.823 --> 00:28:35.453
maybe you need to get
a ladder for the cage

00:28:35.453 --> 00:28:38.336
because parrots like to
climb and get exercise.

00:28:38.336 --> 00:28:40.759
And so she got a ladder
and put it in the cage

00:28:40.759 --> 00:28:43.483
and sat there and watched the parrot.

00:28:43.483 --> 00:28:45.593
Didn't talk so the next day
she went back into the store

00:28:45.593 --> 00:28:47.392
and she said, I got the
ladder, parrot doesn't talk.

00:28:47.392 --> 00:28:50.460
He said, you probably need a swing.

00:28:50.460 --> 00:28:54.846
Parrots like to swing and
just kind of go back and forth

00:28:54.846 --> 00:28:57.569
a little bit, puts 'em in a good mood.

00:28:57.569 --> 00:28:59.704
So she got a swing, put it
in the cage, went back home

00:28:59.704 --> 00:29:03.230
and sat there and watched the parrot.

00:29:03.230 --> 00:29:05.366
The parrot didn't talk.

00:29:05.366 --> 00:29:07.710
Went back to the store
the next day (mumbles).

00:29:07.710 --> 00:29:09.490
Got the swing, got the
ladder, and the parrot still

00:29:09.490 --> 00:29:10.573
doesn't talk.

00:29:13.112 --> 00:29:15.020
He said, you need a mirror.

00:29:15.020 --> 00:29:16.851
(audience laughing)

00:29:16.851 --> 00:29:18.586
A parrot likes to look at himself.

00:29:18.586 --> 00:29:19.890
Get a mirror in there and that'll help.

00:29:19.890 --> 00:29:21.989
So she went and got a
mirror, put it in there

00:29:21.989 --> 00:29:24.114
and the parrot just look at
itself and swing and climb.

00:29:24.114 --> 00:29:27.114
(audience laughing)

00:29:28.078 --> 00:29:31.058
She came back to the manager
the next day and she said,

00:29:31.058 --> 00:29:32.490
the parrot died.

00:29:32.490 --> 00:29:34.470
(audience laughing)

00:29:34.470 --> 00:29:35.671
She said the parrot died.

00:29:35.671 --> 00:29:36.740
Oh how terrible.

00:29:36.740 --> 00:29:39.409
He said, did the parrot say
anything before he died?

00:29:39.409 --> 00:29:42.060
(audience laughing)

00:29:42.060 --> 00:29:44.974
Yeah, said the parrot said,
don't they sell food down there?

00:29:44.974 --> 00:29:47.974
(audience laughing)

00:29:53.154 --> 00:29:54.572
I'm hungry.

00:29:54.572 --> 00:29:56.126
I'm hungry.

00:29:56.126 --> 00:29:57.729
I know all kinds of people
in their spiritual life.

00:29:57.729 --> 00:30:02.623
They got ladders, they got
mirrors, they got swings.

00:30:02.623 --> 00:30:03.873
They got stuff.

00:30:07.064 --> 00:30:09.508
And they don't understand,
they don't understand

00:30:09.508 --> 00:30:11.712
that less is more, that what you got to do

00:30:11.712 --> 00:30:15.355
is go for the simple, go for
the true, go for the food

00:30:15.355 --> 00:30:16.855
for your own soul.

